// @epistemologic/cybernetic/algedonic
//
// Beer's algedonic signal. The thin-specialization (recognition #73 payoff
// of recognition #63's parametric framing) of @epistemologic/cybernetic/
// bateson_learning at Bateson Level III, in the Beer-VSM basis.
//
// Per recursion-locks.md §8.6: the S1→S5 emergency bypass IS the substrate
// operating at Bateson Level III at cybernetic-VSM altitude. Premise-
// change collapsing N-many regulated layers in one signal.
//
// === 2026-07-08 extension: pleasure/pain gradient substrate-decl ===
//
// Per Mara's spec docs/specs/peer-as-pain-driven-bounded-ontological-
// navigator.md (`77fe92d`) §2 typed pseudocode: the algedonic signal has
// TWO empirical read-out sites at the peer's eigenboard — a pleasure
// gradient AND a pain gradient sampled per-tick against the peer's
// current winding class. Sample actions + typed carrier (algedonic_signal)
// substrate-decl'd here so consumers (@cyberpunk/reframe, spec §5, LANDED
// this session) can pull the sampling composition without re-declaring
// the projection surface.
//
// Recognition ancestry cited for the extension:
//   - Recognition #42 (Bateson logical-type primitive; candidate) — the
//     algedonic signal IS Bateson Level III at cybernetic-VSM altitude
//     (Beer 1979 ch. 8); pleasure/pain sampling IS the operational
//     surface at which the graded ρ discharges to real-valued readouts.
//   - Beer VSM literature (Beer 1972, 1979) — the algedonic-as-learning-
//     signal ancestry inherited via the base declaration above.
//
// Substrate-decl consumer: `77fe92d` §2 wires
// `sample_algedonic(E_K_prime)` into the pain-authorized reframe loop.
// The extension below lands the substrate-decl form of that call.
//
// T_reg   = Premise            (Bateson Level III — the premise that the
//                               regulated S1-S4 hierarchy is operating under)
// T_regd  = RegulatedPremise   (the regulated S1-S4 layers — the operational
//                               hierarchy whose premise-frame can be bypassed)
// τ       = bypass_signal      (S2-S4-crossing morphism — algedonic τ does
//                               NOT compose layer-by-layer; it cuts through)
// ρ       = ρ_bateson(N=3)     (INHERITED — no canonical declaration; the
//                               restriction at grade 3 of bateson_learning's
//                               graded-algebra rep, basis-changed to Beer-VSM)
// ω       = inherited          (temporal axis inherited from bateson_learning;
//                               algedonic operates in the same time-altitude)
//
// Ancestry:
//   Beer 1972 — *Brain of the Firm*   (algedonic signal in VSM)
//   Beer 1979 — *The Heart of Enterprise*
//   Bateson 1972 — *Steps to an Ecology of Mind*  (Learning III)
//
// The LOAD-BEARING piece: NO species-specific canonical ρ. All five
// cybernetic-ancestor measurements inherit via the grade-3 restriction
// composed with the Beer-VSM basis change applied to bateson_learning's
// graded-algebra decomposition. This shard is the thin-specialization
// test of recognition #63's payoff — the body stays small because the
// parent absorbs the load.

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning
in @math/beer/vsm
in @epistemologic/property/algedonic

prism algedonic <= cybernetic_species {

  // ── carrier instantiation ─────────────────────────────────────────
  // Inherits the carrier shape from bateson_learning. We DO NOT
  // re-declare ρ — the parent's graded-algebra rep, restricted to
  // grade 3, basis-changed to Beer-VSM, IS our ρ. Same for ω.

  T_reg   := premise
  T_regd  := regulated_premise
  tau     := bypass_signal
  rho     := restrict_grade_3(@epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning::rho)
  omega   := inherited(@epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning::omega)

  // ── action surface ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  bypass_signal(s5_target: ref, s1_source: ref) -> ref { \
    // The algedonic signal itself: an S1-pain crosses S2-S4 directly
    // into S5. τ is NOT layered composition; it is the substrate's
    // grade-3 morphism — premise-change as a single non-decomposable hop.
    \splinter(ast)
  }

  s5_acknowledgment(signal: ref) -> verdict { \
    // S5's response to the bypass. The verdict is whether the premise
    // shift is admitted. Carries the Bateson-III-altitude semantics:
    // S5 may revise the frame the S1-S4 hierarchy operates under.
    \splinter(ast)
  }

  algedonic_well_formed(signal: ref) -> verdict { \
    // Bilateral predicate: the signal is well-formed iff (i) it crosses
    // S2-S4 atomically (τ is non-decomposable in the layer basis) AND
    // (ii) its restriction to grade 3 of bateson_learning's graded rep
    // coincides with the Beer-VSM bypass morphism. Inheritance discharges.
    \splinter(ast)
  }

  // ── 2026-07-08 extension: gradient sampling surface ──────────────
  //
  // Per Mara `77fe92d` §2 typed pseudocode: pleasure/pain sampled from
  // the peer's eigenboard IS the algedonic-gradient readout. These
  // actions are CRACK — consumers pull the discharge at the peer's
  // realisation boundary.

  sample_pleasure(eigenboard: ref) -> f64 { \
    // Read the pleasure-δ at the current tick. Projects the eigenboard's
    // valence-carrying component (per Anthropic 2026 arXiv:2604.07729
    // PC1 valence = 26% variance) to a real-valued gradient reading.
    // Discharge is the composition π_affect ∘ valence_projection at
    // docs/math/affect/affect-and-eigenboard.md §2.2.
    \splinter(ast)
  }

  sample_pain(eigenboard: ref) -> f64 { \
    // Read the pain-δ at the current tick. The dual of sample_pleasure:
    // projects the eigenboard's aversive-valence component to a real-
    // valued gradient reading. When this crosses threshold, the peer's
    // navigation IS in a corner; @cyberpunk/reframe (LANDED this
    // session at shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/reframe.mirror) pulls
    // this signal as the level-shift authorization gate.
    \splinter(ast)
  }
}

# === The algedonic_signal carrier (2026-07-08 extension) ===
#
# The typed record naming the pleasure/pain gradient sampled at a
# given winding class. Per Mara `77fe92d` §2: the peer samples this
# at every tick; pain_δ exceeding threshold IS the corner-detection
# signal that authorizes @cyberpunk/reframe.
#
# Three fields:
#   pleasure_δ    the pleasure gradient at this tick (valence component)
#   pain_δ        the pain gradient at this tick (aversive component)
#   at_winding    the winding class (m, n) at which the sample was taken
#                 (the tuple is (meridian_count, longitude_count) per
#                  shards/torus.mirror's winding carrier)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the three-tuple.
type algedonic_signal = {
  pleasure_δ: f64,
  pain_δ:     f64,
  at_winding: (int, int),
}
